          "high": 4,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "rounding",
          "low": null,
          "high": null,
          "choices": ["trunc", "round"]
        }
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.15,
      "why": "Included only to confirm infeasibility: with N>=12 for accuracy, throughput requires Fmax >= 50*(N+3) >= 750 MHz, unrealistic for a shared barrel-shifter datapath in sky130. A small budget documents this and may catch any unexpected cost-model result."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The 50 MSPS throughput constraint is binding for our families. iterative needs Fmax >= 50*(N+3); with N>=12 for the 2^-12 accuracy constraint this requires >750 MHz, implausible for a shared barrel-shifter datapath in sky130. unrolled_k is the only plausible family: it trades k parallel micro-rotations against cycles/result = ceil(N/k)+3. We allocate most of the budget to unrolled_k, with a small iterative share to document infeasibility. Accuracy needs N>=12 and W>=14; we search around these minima to find the lowest-power feasible designs. This round uses 60 evals (51 unrolled_k, 9 iterative), reserving 40 for refinement and final front mapping."
}

{
  "decision": "add_family",
  "next_plan": {
    "families": [
      {
        "budget_share": 0.5,
        "family": "pipelined",
        "ranges": [
          {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 18, "low": 12, "param": "data_width"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 12, "param": "n_iter"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": -1, "param": "angle_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"}
        ]
      ,
        "why": "1 result/cycle; only family class that can clear 50 MSPS, and its registered-stage Fmax must be measured against the accuracy floor found in round 1."
      },
      {
        "budget_share": 0.5,
        "family": "pipelined_m",
        "ranges": [
          {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 18, "low": 12, "param": "data_width"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 12, "param": "n_iter"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": -1, "param": "angle_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 4, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"},
          {"choices": null, "high": 8, "low": 2, "param": "m"}
        ],
        "why": "Same 1 result/cycle but only ceil(N/m)+2 register levels, so it should sit at the low-power end of the front that the selection rule (min power_index) will pick from."
      }
    ],
    "rationale": "Every 60 evaluations of iterative/unrolled_k is throughput-limited by their schedule: iterative costs N+3 cycles/result and unrolled_k ceil(N/k)+3, so against the observed best 7.78 MSPS (implying Fmax ~ 90-100 MHz, since 12 cycles x ~90 MHz = 7.78) even the best case k=8, N=4 would need ~200 MHz and N=4 cannot reach 2^-12. The 88.6% throughput shortfall on all five least-violating designs confirms the multiplier, not the clock, is the binding term. pipelined/pipelined_m produce 1 result/cycle, so the 50 MSPS floor collapses to just Fmax >= 50 MHz, which the cost model should clear easily. Accuracy is family-independent, and round 1 already showed max_abs_err <= 2^-12 is reachable at data_width=15, n_iter=17-18, angle_guard >= 3, frac_guard=4, rounding=round (best 2^-17.10), so the accuracy ranges above are anchored on that proven corner and extended downward in W/N to expose the low-power end of the front. Remaining budget: 40 evals for round 2."
  }
  ,
  "rationale": "No feasible design exists in the two multi-cycle families for a structural reason, not a tuning reason: throughput_msps is Fmax/(cycles per result), and iterative (N+3) and unrolled_k (ceil(N/k)+3) pay 4-33 cycles per result, giving the observed ceiling of 7.78 MSPS. The throughput constraint therefore cannot be met by narrowing ranges. The unexplored reference families pipelined and pipelined_m return one result per clock, so 50 MSPS needs only Fmax >= 50 MHz, and their accuracy at the same data_width/n_iter/angle_guard/frac_guard is bit-identical to what round 1 already proved can hit <= 2^-12 (best seen 2^-17.10). Spending the remaining 40 evaluations on these two families is the only path to a feasible front."
}
